## Q2: 
Most popular languages like Python, C++, Java, and JavaScript are Turing complete.How?

## A2: 
These languages are Turing complete because they possess the core logical primitives required to simulate any computable function.
## Why They Qualify

* Conditional Branching: They all implement if, else, and switch statements to change execution paths based on data.
* Infinite Loops: They feature while loops, for loops, and recursive function calls to repeat actions indefinitely.
* Arbitrary Storage: They can read, write, and modify variables at any point in memory during execution. [1, 2, 3, 4] 

## The Real-World Distinction
In pure computer science theory, a Turing machine requires an infinite memory tape. Physical computers running Python or Java have finite RAM. Therefore, these languages are technically "linear bounded automata" in practice, but they are universally treated as Turing complete because their software logic places no artificial upper limit on memory scale. [5, 6, 7] 
